- Story & Context: Local legend claims the anomalous signals from the abandoned lighthouse at Blackwater Point never truly stopped, merely shifted beyond human perception, their spectral echo now woven into the very fabric of the polar winds and the groaning ice floes; fishermen report hearing a faint, mournful saxophone when the fog is thickest, a haunting resonance that permeates the air long after the last ship has passed. "The silence isn't empty, it’s just rearranged."
